Sriracha Release Checklist
==========================

See the Sriracha Manual for information on how to install and use Sriracha:
  https://codeberg.org/tslocum/sriracha/src/branch/main/MANUAL.md

This is a checklist of things to do every time a new version of Sriracha is released.

- [ ] Verify git tag is set correctly
- [ ] Run smoke test `sriracha --test`
- [ ] Add 2FA device
- [ ] Log out, log back in using 2FA device
- [ ] Upgrade remote Sriracha instances
- [ ] Verify remote Sriracha instances have not printed any error messages
- [ ] Build for supported platforms `goreleaser --clean --skip=publish`
- [ ] Build and publish Docker container image
  - [ ] `sudo docker build -t tslocum/sriracha:v2.0.0 --build-arg version=2.0.0 .`
  - [ ] `sudo docker tag tslocum/sriracha:v2.0.0 tslocum/sriracha:latest`
  - [ ] `sudo docker push tslocum/sriracha:v2.0.0`
  - [ ] `sudo docker push tslocum/sriracha:latest`
- [ ] Upload release archives to Codeberg
- [ ] Add news entry to official Sriracha instance
